      "content": "In darker skin, melanoma often presents as a flat, non-ulcerated lesion, making it harder to detect. Look for subtle changes in skin texture, such as a slight thickening or hardening of the skin, rather than the typical raised, ulcerated appearance seen in lighter skin. These lesions can be difficult to spot, especially in patients with darker skin tones, as they may blend in with the surrounding skin. It's also crucial to consider the location, as melanomas in darker skin often occur on the palms, soles, or under the nails.",
